# oracle: pppm/dipole with a NON-NEUTRAL charged system (charges 0.1 +- 0.5 alternating by id on 64 sc sites: net charge 6.4, native accepts it with the KSpace::qsum_qsq warning), random dipoles (dipole/random 2261), pair lj/cut/dipole/long 3.5 1.0 (see w168pq_charge_dipole_auto), kspace_style pppm/dipole 1.0e-1 with the automatic G-ewald and mesh, run 0: pe, evdwl, ecoul, elong, press and the per-atom forces, dipoles and torques
# oracle-files: w168pq_nonneutral_tq.dump
# measured with native LAMMPS (/home/roy/.local/bin/lmp, b332f28, installed DIPOLE and KSPACE packages): engine vs native fixture at step 0: max relative error 3.1e-11 (thermo), 1.6e-11 (per-atom forces and positions), 2.3e-11 (dipoles and torques); engine time 4.1 s (Node 24, loaded machine)
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 atomrel=1e-8 filerel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
units           lj
atom_style      hybrid sphere dipole
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
lattice         sc 0.30
region          box block 0 4 0 4 0 4
create_box      1 box
create_atoms    1 box
mass            1 1.0
set             group all diameter 1.0
set             group all density 1.0
variable        qi atom 0.1+((id%2)*2-1)*0.5
set             group all charge v_qi
set             group all dipole/random 2261 1.0
pair_style      lj/cut/dipole/long 3.5 1.0
pair_coeff      1 1 1.0 1.0
kspace_style    pppm/dipole 1.0e-1
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
thermo_style    custom step pe evdwl ecoul elong press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g norm no
thermo          1
run             0
write_dump      all custom w168pq_nonneutral_tq.dump id mux muy muz tqx tqy tqz modify format float %.15g sort id
